// Quotes — RETIRED (consolidated into the Invoicing module's BillingDocument).
//
// The `Quote`/`QuoteItem` models / `quotes`/`quote_items` tables were two
// independently-implemented lifecycles (a CRM path and a separate B2B/RFQ path)
// sharing one table pair. They converged onto `BillingDocument` — the same
// engine that already owns estimates/invoices/receipts — so there is exactly
// one authored-document entity in the platform. Migration
// `<ts>_quotes_to_billing_documents` backfilled every legacy quote into
// `billing_documents` on a system `b2b-quotes` workflow, preserving
// `costCents`/`appliedMarkup` line pricing verbatim and converting the old
// `convertedToOrderId` soft/metadata pointer into a real bidirectional FK
// (`BillingDocument.convertedToOrderId` / `Order.convertedFromDocumentId`).
// Migration `<ts>_drop_quotes` drops the empty tables (expand/contract
// "contract" step), mirroring the `B2bInvoice` → `BillingDocument` precedent
// (see 61-b2b-invoices.prisma).
//
// A quote is now a BillingDocument on the `b2b-quotes` workflow (or any other
// tenant-configured workflow with a `draft`/`committed`-type stage); accepting
// one converts it to an Order via `billingDocumentConversionService.convertToOrder`.
// See:
//   • packages/crm/src/services/billing-document-conversion-service.ts
//   • services/api-rest/src/routes/v1/invoicing/documents.ts (`/convert-to-order`)
//   • packages/crm-schemas/src/builtins/invoicing.ts (B2B_QUOTE_WORKFLOW)
//
// This file intentionally defines no model — kept as a tombstone so the
// retirement is discoverable where the models used to live.
